import AxQM.Postulates.API.DeutschReachableEvolutions
import AxQM.Postulates.API.DeutschGateArbitraryWirePlacement
import AxQM.Concrete.DeutschCompressedUniversality
import ToMathlib.Analysis.CStarAlgebra.MatrixToEuclideanCLM

/-!
# Universality of the Deutsch gate `G = C²(iR_x(πα))` with ancillas
(N&C Exercise 4.44 — the density transport + the `deutschGate α` naming)

The matrix development of Exercise 4.44 establishes universality *with ancillas* at the level of raw
matrices: for `α` irrational, the data-register actions of `G`-placement circuits with ancillas held
`|1⟩` — the compressed circuits `Concrete.deutschDataReachableCircuits` — are dense in `U(2ⁿ)` up to
a global phase (`Concrete.exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschDataReachableCircuits`). Two further
steps lift that to a statement about the *physical* gate `deutschGate α`
(`= ccontrolledUnitary (iRxGate (πα))`, an `Evolution`):

* **transport** — the full-register reachable circuit matrices are the operators of a submonoid of
  register `Evolution`s (`deutschReachableEvolutions`,
  `AxQM/Postulates/API/DeutschReachableEvolutions.lean`),
  so the matrix density transports through the continuous `⋆`-algebra isomorphism
  `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM` onto the compressed operators of that `Evolution` submonoid; and
* **naming** — the exact base `G`-placements among the generators of `deutschReachableEvolutions`
  are the physical Deutsch gate `deutschGate α` conjugated onto register wires (the arbitrary-triple
  naming `quditGate_mcCtrlSingleQubit_distinct_eq_conj_congr_tmul_ccontrolledUnitary`), so
  the submonoid the density statement is about is genuinely generated by `deutschGate α`.

## What is formalised

* `dataRegisterOp ι E` — the **data-register action** of a full-register evolution
  `E : Evolution (qudit D)`: the operator on the data space `EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin d)` obtained by
  compressing `E`'s operator matrix to the ancilla-`|1⟩` coordinate subspace `range ι`
  (`Concrete.compress`) and re-promoting through `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM`. This is the physical
  observable of a `G`-circuit run with its ancillas held `|1⟩`. `dataRegisterOp_eq` reads it off
  from a known operator matrix.
* `exists_phase_smul_toEuclideanCLM_mem_closure_dataRegisterOp_deutschReachableEvolutions` — **the
  density transport** (`α` irrational, `≥ 1` data qubit, `≥ 2` ancillas): for any `U ∈ U(2ⁿ)` some
  global phase `e^{ia}` makes `e^{ia} • Matrix.toEuclideanCLM U` a limit of the data-register
  actions `dataRegisterOp ι '' deutschReachableEvolutions` — the physical `G`-circuits with
  ancillas are dense in the data-register unitaries up to an (unobservable) global phase. The
  Deutsch-gate counterpart of Exercise 4.43's
  `exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_reachableCircuitEvolutions`.
* `exists_conj_ccontrolledUnitary_mem_deutschReachableEvolutions` — **the naming**: an actual base
  `G`-placement is a generator of `deutschReachableEvolutions`, and equals `deutschGate α`
  (`ccontrolledUnitary (iRxGate (πα))`, its unfolded form here) transported to `qudit 8`, tensored
  with the identity, and conjugated by the register-permutation gate `quditPerm ρ`. So the physical
  Deutsch gate really does generate the universal submonoid.

The register submonoid it transports onto is in
`AxQM/Postulates/API/DeutschReachableEvolutions.lean`.
-/

open Matrix

namespace AxQM

noncomputable section

open AxQM.Concrete

/-- **The data-register action of a full-register evolution.** For `E : Evolution (qudit D)`, the
operator on the data space obtained by compressing `E`'s operator matrix
`(Matrix.toEuclideanCLM).symm E.op` to the ancilla-`|1⟩` coordinate subspace `range ι`
(`Concrete.compress ι`) and re-promoting through `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM`. When the ancillas are held
`|1⟩` (the subspace `range ι` picks out), `dataRegisterOp ι E` is exactly the operator `E` induces
on the data register — the physical observable of the `G`-circuit `E` run with ancillas. -/
def dataRegisterOp {D d : ℕ} (ι : Fin d → Fin D) (E : Evolution (qudit D)) :
    EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin d) →L[ℂ] EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin d) :=
  Matrix.toEuclideanCLM (𝕜 := ℂ) (n := Fin d)
    (compress ι ((Matrix.toEuclideanCLM (𝕜 := ℂ) (n := Fin D)).symm E.op))

/-- **Reading off `dataRegisterOp` from a known operator matrix.** If `E.op = Matrix.toEuclideanCLM
N`, then `dataRegisterOp ι E = Matrix.toEuclideanCLM (compress ι N)` — the compression of the known
matrix `N`, re-promoted. Immediate from `StarAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply` (`Matrix.toEuclideanCLM` is
a `⋆`-algebra isomorphism, so its inverse undoes it). -/
theorem dataRegisterOp_eq {D d : ℕ} (ι : Fin d → Fin D) {E : Evolution (qudit D)}
    {N : Matrix (Fin D) (Fin D) ℂ}
    (hN : E.op = Matrix.toEuclideanCLM (𝕜 := ℂ) (n := Fin D) N) :
    dataRegisterOp ι E = Matrix.toEuclideanCLM (𝕜 := ℂ) (n := Fin d) (compress ι N) := by
  rw [dataRegisterOp, hN, StarAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply]

/-- **Universality of the Deutsch gate `G` with ancillas** (Nielsen & Chuang,
Exercise 4.44). When `α` is irrational, the data register has at least one qubit
(`[Nontrivial (Fin m → Fin 2)]`) and at least two ancillas (`a₀ ≠ a₁ : Fin n`), for *any* unitary
`U ∈ U(2ⁿ)` some global phase `e^{ia}` makes

  `e^{ia} • Matrix.toEuclideanCLM U
    ∈ closure (dataRegisterOp ι '' deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α)`

with `ι = Concrete.regEmbed fullEnc dataEnc e` the ancilla-`|1⟩` embedding: the data-register
actions of the register `G`-circuit evolutions `deutschReachableEvolutions` are dense in the
data-register unitaries up to an (unobservable) global phase.

The matrix headline `Concrete.exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschDataReachableCircuits` supplies
`a` with `e^{ia} • U` a limit of the compressed circuit matrices
`deutschDataReachableCircuits = compress ι '' deutschAncillaReachableCircuits`. Pushing this through
the continuous `⋆`-algebra isomorphism `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM` (`Matrix.continuous_toEuclideanCLM`,
`image_closure_subset_closure_image`), which — being `ℂ`-linear — commutes with the phase
(`map_smul`), lands `e^{ia} • Matrix.toEuclideanCLM U` in the closure of
`Matrix.toEuclideanCLM '' deutschDataReachableCircuits`. Finally each compressed matrix
`compress ι N` (`N ∈ deutschAncillaReachableCircuits`) is `dataRegisterOp ι E` for a member `E` of
`deutschReachableEvolutions` whose operator is `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM N`
(`exists_deutschReachableEvolution_op_eq`, `dataRegisterOp_eq`), so that image sits inside the
data-register-action image of the submonoid, and `closure_mono` concludes. The Deutsch-gate
counterpart of Exercise 4.43's `exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_reachableCircuitEvolutions`. -/
theorem exists_phase_smul_toEuclideanCLM_mem_closure_dataRegisterOp_deutschReachableEvolutions
    {M m n D d : ℕ} (fullEnc : (Fin M → Fin 2) ≃ Fin D)
    (dataEnc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d) (e : Fin M ≃ Fin m ⊕ Fin n)
    [Nontrivial (Fin m → Fin 2)] {α : ℝ} (hα : Irrational α) (a₀ a₁ : Fin n) (ha : a₀ ≠ a₁)
    {U : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ} (hU : U ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (Fin d) ℂ) :
    ∃ a : ℝ,
      Complex.exp ((a : ℂ) * Complex.I) • Matrix.toEuclideanCLM (𝕜 := ℂ) (n := Fin d) U ∈
        closure (dataRegisterOp (regEmbed fullEnc dataEnc e) ''
          (deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α : Set (Evolution (qudit D)))) := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha'⟩ := exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschDataReachableCircuits
    fullEnc dataEnc e hα a₀ a₁ ha hU
  refine ⟨a, ?_⟩
  -- Transport the matrix membership through the continuous map `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM`.
  have h1 := image_closure_subset_closure_image
    (Matrix.continuous_toEuclideanCLM (𝕜 := ℂ) (n := Fin d))
    (Set.mem_image_of_mem (fun M => Matrix.toEuclideanCLM (𝕜 := ℂ) (n := Fin d) M) ha')
  -- `toEuclideanCLM` is `ℂ`-linear, so it commutes with the global phase.
  simp only [map_smul] at h1
  -- Every compressed circuit matrix is the data-register action of a register-submonoid member.
  refine closure_mono ?_ h1
  rintro _ ⟨M, hM, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨N, hN, rfl⟩ := hM
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hEop⟩ := exists_deutschReachableEvolution_op_eq (SetLike.mem_coe.mp hN)
  exact ⟨E, hE, dataRegisterOp_eq _ hEop⟩

/-- **The physical Deutsch gate `G` generates the universal register submonoid** (Nielsen & Chuang,
Exercise 4.44, the naming). For a register encoding `fullEnc : (Fin M → Fin 2) ≃ Fin (8·r)`, a
`rest`-encoding `restEnc : (Fin (M - 3) → Fin 2) ≃ Fin r`, a data encoding
`dataEnc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d`, a data-ancilla split `e : Fin M ≃ Fin m ⊕ Fin n`, two distinct
ancillas `a₀ ≠ a₁` and a data wire `j`, there is a member of
`deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α` equal to the physical Deutsch gate `deutschGate α`
(`= ccontrolledUnitary (iRxGate (πα))`, its unfolded form) transported to `qudit 8`, tensored with
the identity, and conjugated by the register-permutation gate `quditPerm ρ`.

It is the base `G`-placement with controls on the two ancillas `a₀, a₁` (held `|1⟩`) and target on
the data wire `j`: this placement is ancilla-preserving (`mcCtrlSingleQubit_dataTarget_mem_...`, its
target is a data wire) and a genuine `G`-iterate
(`iR_x(πα) = iRxMat (πα)^1 ∈ deutschTargetOrbit α`), hence a generator of
`deutschReachableEvolutions` (`quditGate_mem_deutschReachableEvolutions`); and
the arbitrary-triple naming
(`quditGate_mcCtrlSingleQubit_distinct_eq_conj_congr_tmul_ccontrolledUnitary`) identifies its
promotion with the conjugated `deutschGate α`. -/
theorem exists_conj_ccontrolledUnitary_mem_deutschReachableEvolutions {M m n r d : ℕ}
    (fullEnc : (Fin M → Fin 2) ≃ Fin (8 * r)) (restEnc : (Fin (M - 3) → Fin 2) ≃ Fin r)
    (dataEnc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d) (e : Fin M ≃ Fin m ⊕ Fin n) (α : ℝ)
    (a₀ a₁ : Fin n) (ha : a₀ ≠ a₁) (j : Fin m) :
    ∃ e₃ : Fin M ≃ Fin 3 ⊕ Fin (M - 3),
      quditPerm (fullEnc.symm.trans (regTensorEnc e₃ restEnc)).symm
          * Evolution.congr (quditProdIso 8 r).symm
              ((Evolution.congr threeQuditIso
                (ccontrolledUnitary (iRxGate (Real.pi * α)))).tmul Evolution.id)
          * quditPerm (fullEnc.symm.trans (regTensorEnc e₃ restEnc))
        ∈ deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α := by
  -- Wire roles: controls on the two ancillas `a₀, a₁`, target on the data wire `j`; all distinct.
  have hAB : e.symm (Sum.inr a₀) ≠ e.symm (Sum.inr a₁) :=
    fun h => ha (Sum.inr_injective (e.symm.injective h))
  have hAJ : e.symm (Sum.inr a₀) ≠ e.symm (Sum.inl j) :=
    fun h => Sum.inr_ne_inl (e.symm.injective h)
  have hBJ : e.symm (Sum.inr a₁) ≠ e.symm (Sum.inl j) :=
    fun h => Sum.inr_ne_inl (e.symm.injective h)
  -- The base `G`-placement is an ancilla-preserving reachable gate.
  have hmem : mcCtrlSingleQubit fullEnc {e.symm (Sum.inr a₀), e.symm (Sum.inr a₁)}
      (e.symm (Sum.inl j)) (iRxMat (Real.pi * α))
      ∈ deutschAncillaReachableGates fullEnc dataEnc e α := by
    refine ⟨mcCtrlSingleQubit_dataTarget_mem_compressionInvariant fullEnc dataEnc e _ j _,
      e.symm (Sum.inr a₀), e.symm (Sum.inr a₁), e.symm (Sum.inl j),
      subset_closure (Set.mem_image_of_mem _ ?_)⟩
    have hpow : iRxMat (Real.pi * α) = iRxMat (Real.pi * α) ^ 1 := (pow_one _).symm
    rw [hpow]
    exact iRxMat_pow_mem_deutschTargetOrbit α 1
  -- Its promotion is a generator of the register submonoid...
  have hgen := quditGate_mem_deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α hmem
  -- ...and equals the conjugated physical Deutsch gate (arbitrary-triple naming).
  obtain ⟨e₃, heq⟩ :=
    quditGate_mcCtrlSingleQubit_distinct_eq_conj_congr_tmul_ccontrolledUnitary
      fullEnc restEnc hAB hAJ hBJ α
  refine ⟨e₃, ?_⟩
  rw [← heq]
  exact hgen

end

end AxQM
